  "verdict": {
    "text": "Cambodia pledges a 41.7% reduction by 2030 against 2030 BAU. A later submission, Cambodia’s NDC 3.0, was filed on 2025-08-08; it has not been read, so no figure here comes from it. The document conditions its targets on international support but publishes no numeric split, so none is shown. 49 observed values are loaded from DS-02 (11), DS-06-NDC (1), DS-35 (35), DS-40 (2). For 2024 the sources disagree: DS-35 91.8 MtCO₂e, DS-02 47.7 MtCO₂e. They are on different inventory scopes and the engine does not reconcile them. The target is not reached on the observed trend. It submitted BTR1 on 2024-12-31. 0 of 8 components have been confirmed in the document; the rest are unparsed, which is not a finding against the country. ND-GAIN scores it 42.4 for 2024. In the first NDC round, WRI's CAIT assessment recorded: 27% reduction in GHG emissions by 2030 compared to the BAU scenario, as well as a LULUCF contribution of 4.7 tCO2e/ha/year. It was classed conditional. That is a 2016 assessment of an earlier submission, not the target above. Projected warming for 2080-2099 against 1995-2014 ranges from +1.18°C under SSP1-2.6 to +3.81°C under SSP5-8.5. These are model runs, not observations.",
